title: Aurora Pyramid Requisition
subtitle: Housing emergency
priority: 2
max-visits: 1
tags: event
new-page: true
view-if: month >= 8 and year = 2302 and third_wave_on_society = 1 and aurora_pyramid_housing_event = 0
on-arrival: aurora_pyramid_housing_event = 1

The refugee wave has outstripped every spare bunk in Mikasa.  Squatter camps spread through Aurora's public corridors while the city council argues over budgets it does not really have.  Finally someone points at the obvious landmark: the forbidden Aurora Pyramid, hollow and half-ruined since the bank vanished, yet still plumbed, still on the municipal grid, and still tall enough to swallow a small district's worth of people.

Independent contractors and long-term squatters protest that the pyramid is *their* commons now.  The Aurora district council — one of the few bodies with real local legitimacy — votes to requisition it anyway.  Engineers estimate the structure can be partitioned into several public housing sites without waiting for megacorp salvage rights to clear.

- @public_housing: Requisition the pyramid for public housing
- @defer: Stall — keep negotiating with the squatters
- @ica_lease: Lease the pyramid to the Independent Contractors Association

@public_housing
title: Requisition the pyramid for public housing
on-arrival: {!
aurora_pyramid_public_housing = 1;
Q.addHome({ id: 'aurora_pyramid_atrium', name: 'Grand atrium housing block', district: 'Aurora', ownerType: 'public', owner: 'city', housingFor: 'third_wave', major: true });
Q.addHome({ id: 'aurora_pyramid_vault_tiers', name: 'Vault tier dormitories', district: 'Aurora', ownerType: 'public', owner: 'city', housingFor: 'third_wave', major: true });
Q.addHome({ id: 'aurora_pyramid_apex_wings', name: 'Apex wing public suites', district: 'Aurora', ownerType: 'public', owner: 'city', housingFor: 'third_wave', major: false });
Q.addHome({ id: 'aurora_pyramid_basement', name: 'Basement grav-bunk housing', district: 'Aurora', ownerType: 'public', owner: 'city', housingFor: 'third_wave', major: false });
Q.addHome({ id: 'aurora_pyramid_otherworld_annex', name: 'Otherworld arrival annex', district: 'Aurora', ownerType: 'public', owner: 'city', housingFor: 'alien', major: true });
!}

Work crews seal the worst structural cracks, strip out bank-era security hardpoints, and partition the pyramid's vast interior into dormitory stacks.  Third-wave refugees fill the upper tiers; Otherworld arrivals get the annex nearest the district's stable gate.  Children still shout in the echoing halls — but now they do it under city leases instead of squatter truces.

[? if jovian_refugee_prepare = 1: Relief organizers credit the earlier refugee-prep push for having survey teams ready. ?]

@defer
title: Stall — keep negotiating with the squatters
on-arrival: aurora_pyramid_housing_deferred = 1

The council kicks the decision down the road.  Squatters and ICA freelancers keep the pyramid as a patchwork commune while refugees pile up in Aurora's parks.  TODO: follow-up event or timed re-trigger when `aurora_pyramid_housing_deferred = 1`.

@ica_lease
title: Lease the pyramid to the Independent Contractors Association
on-arrival: aurora_pyramid_ica_lease = 1

The Independent Contractors Association wins a long-term lease and promises "adaptive mixed-use redevelopment."  TODO: `Q.addAsset` workshop sites instead of public homes; electorate modifiers for Aurora independents vs refugee advocates.

